{
  "about": [
    "States of a dashboard view as written, each with what the server reads in it (F154.2, F159).",
    "An entry that reads has its normal form, the state after #dash/ in the address the server answers, its look-only parts as that form writes them, and its notes where it has any, one per part dropped.",
    "It has the query it means too, the planner's: its time, a range by its key as written, else its spans as instants in UTC, each end exclusive; its By, color and focus; its scope, each drill level, each chip on a dimension's values and each condition on each item as a chip writes it, a quick filter that is on as its chip; each measure with its fact and the part its items are, or why it is refused and what stands in for it, a ratio with its two; its statements, a grouped scan per fact, a statement per fact and grain over a part's items and, where a chip marks, a statement of the marked rows per fact, each with its groupings, the joins it reads and each dimension or item condition it reads through another fact's conversations; its marks, the marked chips with no mark; each threshold on the By's rows with what it keeps or marks and its measure; and whether the outlier rows' chip keeps or marks.",
    "An entry with a fault has the refusal's exact text, a line an item.",
    "The backend's suite reads every entry through GET /api/dashboard/address's service (tests/dashboard/test_states.py), on the suite's database, whose quota weeks start on 2 January 2025."
  ],
